codex
The pinned artifacts already overturn part of the prior audit: `pi-agent-core@0.80.7` publicly exports `SessionStorage`, `Session`, and `AgentHarness`; `pi-coding-agent@0.80.7` also exposes `SessionManager.inMemory()`. I’m now testing the stronger claim—whether a host-owned adapter can survive process boundaries and drive real turns without any default-session file writes.
